  "implementation": [
    "World prepares Stagger31 resources for NPC and paired Player views, including sheathed actors. Each source descriptor captures actual locomotion coordinates, frequency, cycle and view clock. A view with no slot0 source activates immediately in NI state1; a steady source crossfades in state2.",
    "Typed contact publication rejects stale/malformed descriptors and requires canonical outgoing histories atomically. Existing slot3 attack/reaction phases remain independent; canceled pending contacts are consumed once.",
    "Renderer selects lower-body locomotion ahead of an upper-body idle, excludes slot3/4 tracks from adoption, and suppresses legacy slot0 background while Stagger owns it.",
    "Canonicalized clamp phase adoption avoids a one-float-step false rewind at frame zero. Existing schema59 storage is unchanged."
  ],
